	Section:
		Text: Tables
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: Basic table
		Paragraph: A `Table` has `Header rows` (optional), `Body rows` and `Footer rows` (optional), in that order, each with its `Row` elements and each row with its `Cell` elements from left to right. `Column sizes` is required, and every row fills all the columns exactly. An empty cell is written `Cell:` with nothing after it.
			Style: intro
		Table:
			Column sizes: * 60 80 80
			Column align: left right right right
			Header rows:
				Row:
					Cell: Item
					Cell: Qty
					Cell: Price
					Cell: Amount
			Body rows:
				Row:
					Cell: Walnut chair
					Cell: 12
					Cell: 145.00
					Cell: 1,740.00
				Row:
					Cell: Dining table
					Cell: 1
					Cell: 890.00
					Cell: 890.00
				Row:
					Cell: Delivery
					Cell:
					Cell:
					Cell: 0.00
